# What a person reviews because proofs cannot: specs, trusted code, the C, CI and infrastructure,
# and decisions (CONTRIBUTING.md). Everything else is evidenced by proofs, checks and tests, and
# has no owner here on purpose. Globs rather than paths where the tree may move.

# Trusted code and what it is built and run with.
/TRUSTED.md       @nathanrs
/native/          @nathanrs
/lakefile.lean    @nathanrs
/.github/         @nathanrs
/infra/           @nathanrs
# The adapters' IO and the shell: each area keeps what performs IO in an `IO/` directory.
/Lanes/**/IO/     @nathanrs
# Trusted code outside an `IO/` directory (TRUSTED.md): the wire format and its grammar, the
# template macro, and the declarations of the C.
/Lanes/Web/Http/Wire.lean           @nathanrs
/Lanes/Web/Http/Grammar.lean        @nathanrs
/Lanes/Web/Html/Syntax.lean         @nathanrs
/Lanes/Lib/Crypto/Native.lean       @nathanrs
/Lanes/Lib/Crypto/Sign.lean         @nathanrs
/Lanes/Lib/Crypto/Verify.lean       @nathanrs

# Decisions.
/docs/decisions/  @nathanrs

# Specs: the applications' (`Spec.lean`), the wire format's
# (`WireSpec.lean`), the models of what the outside may do (`Lanes/Outside/`, the typed store's,
# the services' and a shared cache's), which proofs about data rest on (D110), and the
# behaviours, whose specs sit with them.
**/*Spec.lean     @nathanrs
/Lanes/Outside/   @nathanrs
/Lanes/Db/Model.lean                  @nathanrs
/Lanes/Services/**/*Model.lean        @nathanrs
/Lanes/Services/Stripe/Payments.lean  @nathanrs
/Lanes/Web/Http/SharedCache.lean      @nathanrs
**/Behaviours/    @nathanrs
